e reset helper $8EE6/$8EE9.\n\nBut to be accurate about which code writes \"the new scroll\", I should present both and note the order. Let me verify the order of $2005 writes within a frame and the $2000 writes by disassembling the NMI. Let me disassemble $8082 to $8150 (CPU 32898..33104). That's 206 bytes — disassemble length 208.\n\nActually disassemble tool failed earlier for some addresses but worked for 36560. Let me try 32898 (0x8082).\n\nAlso read $0778.\n\nLet me also record a nice \"before\" and \"after\" screenshot. I have before (start) and after (scrolled). Good.\n\nLet me disassemble the NMI to confirm order: does the NMI write 0,0 via $80AB JSR $8EE6 early, and where's the VRAM buffer read? Let me just disassemble 0x8082 length 0xCF (207). Might be long output but fine.\n\nLet me do: disassemble 32898 length 200; read $0778 (1912); read $2000? can't read write-only. \n\nLet me go."}
