{"type":"text","text":"## The status-bar scroll split, proven\n\n**Scanline:** the split is at **scanline 31**. Screen scanlines 0–31 (top 4 tile rows, y 0–31) are the fixed HUD at scroll 0,0 in nametable 0; scanline 32 down is the level at scroll_x = the camera, nametable 1. `get_tile_at_pixel` at y=8/24/30/31 reports `scroll_source:\"vblank\"`, scroll_x 0; at y=32/40/100/200 it reports `scroll_source:\"scanline\"`, `scroll_scanline:31`, scroll_x 1 (camera was `$071A/$071C` = 257).\n\n**What it waits for:** the **sprite‑0 hit** — PPUSTATUS `$2002` bit 6. Gated by `$0722` (=1 in 1‑1), the NMI runs this loop at `$8150`:\n```\n$8150  LDA $2002\n$8153  AND #$40\n$8155  BEQ $8150     ; loop ~190×/frame until the hit\n```\nSprite 0 is OAM #0: tile `$FF` at (88,25), palette 7 — the invisible HUD‑coin sprite, whose only opaque pixels are rows 5–6 = scanlines 30–31 over the HUD coin tile `$2E`. `trace_writes read` on `$2002` (3 frames, 585 reads) shows the reader at `$8153` with value `$1E` until it exits on `$5E` (bit `$40` set).\n\n**Which code writes the new scroll** — the NMI at `$815C`–`$816C`, after a 20‑iteration delay (`$8157 LDY #$14 / DEY / BNE`):\n```\n$815C  LDA $073F ; $815F STA $2005   <- horizontal scroll = camera low byte\n$8162  LDA $0740 ; $8165 STA $2005   <- vertical scroll = 0\n$8168  LDA $0778 ; $816C STA $2000   <- PPUCTRL: nametable select -> 1\n```\nThe **fixed top** is written earlier in the same NMI: `$808C` sets `$2000` with nametable 0, and `$80A9–$80AD` does `LDA #$00 / JSR $8EE6` — the helper at `$8EE6` is `STA $2005 / STA $2005 / RTS`, i.e. the status bar's 0,0 scroll. So the NMI sets scroll 0,0 for the HUD, blocks in the sprite‑0 wait through scanlines 0–31, then switches scroll (and nametable) at scanline 31.\n\n**Evidence:** `trace_writes` on `$2005` at camera 0 gave 4 writers, all value 0; re-run at camera 257 gave pc `$8162` value 1 and pc `$8168` value 0 (once per frame) plus the helper's `$8EE9`/`$8EEC` writing 0,0. Before/after screenshots: HUD `MARIO 000000 / WORLD 1-1 / TIME 394` at camera 0, then `MARIO 000100 / WORLD 1-1 / TIME 235` at camera 257 — bar unmoved, level scrolled.\n\nRecorded as note `scroll split` and promoted to the ROM mapping file."}
